Sval: restore a window's default title bar before destroying it

On Windows 11, nsWindow::SetCustomTitlebar has the Windows App SDK collapse
the title bar (WindowsUIUtils::SetIsTitlebarCollapsed, which sets
ExtendsContentIntoTitleBar). The SDK keeps that title bar's GDI objects
after the window is destroyed: about twenty per window, in every Firefox
channel. A process that opens and closes a few hundred windows reaches
Windows' limit of 10,000 GDI objects, and the next window's title bar fails
inside the SDK, which fail-fasts (e0464645 in
Microsoft.UI.Windowing.Core.dll). Restoring the default title bar
(ResetToDefault) before DestroyWindow frees them.

diff --git a/widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp b/widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp
index 65e81fef82..11b54d3cc7 100644
--- a/widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp
+++ b/widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp
@@ -1320,6 +1320,12 @@ void nsWindow::Destroy() {
    */
   DestroyLayerManager();
 
+  // The Windows App SDK keeps a collapsed title bar's resources past the
+  // window's destruction; restoring the default title bar first frees them.
+  if (mCustomNonClient && ShouldAssociateWithWinAppSDK()) {
+    WindowsUIUtils::SetIsTitlebarCollapsed(mWnd, false);
+  }
+
